adjudication.rationale:
In packages/core/EventManager.ts the diff changes a safe optional-chain check into an unsafe property access:

```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```

When `evt.destinationCalendar` is `undefined`, `null`, or `[]`, destructuring yields `mainHostDestinationCalendar === undefined`. Accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a TypeError. The preceding comment indicates this path is meant to handle the case where Google Meet is selected without a Google Calendar (i.e., destinationCalendar may be missing), so the crash is a verifiable defect introduced by the diff (though the finding’s mention of “Cal-Video bookings” is slightly imprecise; the crash triggers when `evt.location === MeetLocationType`).

In `packages/core/EventManager.ts`, the diff changes the Google Meet fallback logic to:
```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  evt["location"] = "integrations:daily";
}
```
If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `null`, `undefined`, or an empty array, `mainHostDestinationCalendar` becomes `undefined`, and the subsequent `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` dereference will throw `Cannot read properties of undefined`. This is a concrete runtime defect introduced by the change, and it can occur for Meet bookings that don't have a destination calendar set (or when it’s empty).

In EventManager.ts the diff introduces:
```ts
const [mainHostDestinationCalendar] = evt.destinationCalendar ?? [];
if (evt.location === MeetLocationType && mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration !== "google_calendar") {
  ...
}
```
If `evt.destinationCalendar` is `undefined`, `null`, or `[]`, then `mainHostDestinationCalendar` is `undefined`, and accessing `mainHostDestinationCalendar.integration` will throw a runtime TypeError. The `?? []` only protects the destructuring, not the subsequent property access. This is a concrete crash scenario introduced by the change to make `destinationCalendar` an array.
